Package: bartEffTox
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Nonparametric EffTox Design for Phase I/II Dose Finding
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2025-05-09
Authors@R: c(
    person("[Author names redacted for review]", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "[email redacted]"))
Description: Implements the BART-EffTox design for Bayesian Phase I/II
    oncology dose-finding trials. The design extends the EffTox decision
    framework (Thall and Cook 2004) by replacing the parametric bivariate
    dose-response model with separate probit Bayesian Additive Regression
    Trees (BART) models for efficacy and toxicity, combined at the decision
    stage through a common efficacy-toxicity utility function. A
    pool-adjacent-violators (PAVA) isotonic projection enforces monotone
    toxicity at each decision stage without constraining the efficacy
    surface. The package provides functions for: run-in beta-binomial
    safety calibration; PAVA isotonic projection; BART-phase admissibility
    and utility-based dose selection; full two-phase trial simulation; and
    operating characteristic summarisation. A retrospective illustration
    using published AML trial summaries from Thall and Cook (2004) is
    included.
